    <string name="note_current_from_request">This is the current that was agreed, taken from the request object, not a measurement. The voltage that would go with it needs the charger\'s object list, which this kernel did not read.</string>
    <string name="note_measured_not_agreed">This is what is being delivered rather than what was asked for: the upstream interface publishes no request object.</string>
    <string name="note_no_capabilities">The kernel created the power delivery devices but registered no capabilities in them, so the object list is not available. With UCSI that happens when the firmware does not report PDO details, or when the platform skips reading the charger\'s objects. Nothing in userspace can recover them.</string>
    <string name="note_unavailable">No power delivery interface was found. The list needs either Qualcomm\'s own driver at /sys/class/usbpd or the upstream class at /sys/class/usb_power_delivery, and this kernel publishes neither.</string>

    <string name="root_needed">Root access is needed to read these files on this ROM, and it was not granted.</string>
